m/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-16T12:01:39Z","updated_at":"2026-04-16T12:01:39Z","body":"We don't reopen tickets that are this old, we need a new ticket with reference and all the required debug data so we can replicate it. There is no way for us to meaningfully find the bug from what is in here.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4259891387/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4439510460","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/1637#issuecomment-4439510460","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/1637","id":4439510460,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz888AAAABCJ2NvA","user":{"login":"pva","id":92356,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyMzU2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92356?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pva","html_url":"https://github.com/pva","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pva/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pva/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pva/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pva/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pva/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pva/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pva/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pva/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pva/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T09:37:25Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T09:37:25Z","body":"Looks like I found workabound. @kradalby could you comment, please?\n\n## Problem description\n\nThere are two nodes in a Headscale/Tailscale network:\n\n### `node1` — exit node\n\n```text\nInternal IP: 10.1.0.2/24\nExternal IP: 88.88.88.2/24\nExternal subnet: 88.88.88.0/24\n```\n\n### `node2` — client\n\n```text\nInternal IP: 10.2.0.2/24\n```\n\nWhen `node2` uses `node1` as an exit node, general Internet access works as expected.  \nFor example, access to external addresses such as `8.8.8.8` works.\n\nHowever, `node2` cannot access other addresses from the same external subnet that is directly connected to `node1`.\n\nExample:\n\n```bash\n# Before enabling node1 as exit node\nnode2$ ping -c1 88.88.88.3\n# OK\n\nnode2$ ping -c1 8.8.8.8\n# OK\n\n# Enable node1 as exit node\nnode2$ tailscale up --exit-node=node1 --accept-routes --login-server=https://vpn.example.com\n\n# After enabling node1 as exit node\nnode2$ ping -c1 88.88.88.3\n# FAIL\n\nnode2$ ping -c1 8.8.8.8\n# Still OK\n```\n\nSo the problem is not with exit-node forwarding in general.  \nThe problem appears only for destinations that belong to the external subnet directly connected to the exit node itself, in this example:\n\n```text\n88.88.88.0/24\n```\n\n## Cause\n\nWhen `node2` selects `node1` as the exit node, all external IPv4 traffic from `node2` is routed through the Tailscale default route: `0.0.0.0/0`. Therefore, a packet from `node2` to `88.88.88.3` is sent via `tailscale0` and delivered through WireGuard to `node1`.\n\nWhen Tailscale builds the inbound filter for a node advertising an exit node, it explicitly subtracts locally reachable interface networks of the exit node from the advertised default route.\n\nRelevant code:\n\n`tailscale/ipn/ipnlocal/local.go`, around line `2997`:\n\n```go\nif prefs.Valid() {\n    if buildfeatures.HasAdvertiseRoutes {\n        for _, r := range prefs.AdvertiseRoutes().All() {\n            if r.Bits() == 0 {\n                // When offering a default route to the world, we\n                // filter out locally reachable LANs, so that the\n                // default route effectively appears to be a \"guest\n                // wifi\": you get internet access, but to additionally\n                // get LAN access the LAN(s) need to be offered\n                // explicitly as well.\n                localInterfaceRoutes, hostIPs, err := interfaceRoutes()\n                if err != nil {\n                    b.logf(\"getting local interface routes: %v\", err)\n                    continue\n                }\n                s, err := shrinkDefaultRoute(r, localInterfaceRoutes, hostIPs)\n                if err != nil {\n                    b.logf(\"computing default route filter: %v\", err)\n                    continue\n                }\n                localNetsB.AddSet(s)\n```\n\nOn `node1`, the external interface has: `88.88.88.2/24`. Therefore, the whole network is treated as a locally connected network of the exit node.\n\nInside `shrinkDefaultRoute`, this local interface network is removed from the allowed default route. Then only the host's own IP address, `88.88.88.2`, is added back. But neighbouring addresses from the same subnet, e.g. `88.88.88.3` are not added back. Relevant code:\n\n`tailscale/ipn/ipnlocal/local.go`, around line `3237`:\n\n```go\n// shrinkDefaultRoute returns an IPSet representing the IPs in route,\n// minus those in removeFromDefaultRoute and localInterfaceRoutes,\n// plus the IPs in hostIPs.\nfunc shrinkDefaultRoute(route netip.Prefix, localInterfaceRoutes *netipx.IPSet, hostIPs []netip.Addr) (*netipx.IPSet, error) {\n    var b netipx.IPSetBuilder\n    // Add the default route.\n    b.AddPrefix(route)\n    // Remove the local interface routes.\n    b.RemoveSet(localInterfaceRoutes)\n\n    // Having removed all the LAN subnets, re-add the hosts's own\n    // IPs. It's fine for clients to connect to an exit node's public\n    // IP address, just not the attached subnet.\n    //\n    // Truly forbidden subnets (in removeFromDefaultRoute) will still\n    // be stripped back out by the next step.\n    for _, ip := range hostIPs {\n        if route.Contains(ip) {\n            b.Add(ip)\n        }\n    }\n\n    for _, pfx := range removeFromDefaultRoute {\n        b.RemovePrefix(pfx)\n    }\n    return b.IPSet()\n}\n```\n\nAfter the packet is decrypted on `node1`, the inbound filter checks whether the destination address belongs to a network that this node is allowed to receive from Tailscale. For destination `88.88.88.3`, this check fails, because `88.88.88.0/24` was removed from the effective default route and was not explicitly advertised as a subnet route.\n\nAs a result, the packet is dropped inside `tailscaled`.\n\n## Proposed workaround / solution that works for us\n\nOn the exit node, explicitly advertise the external subnet:\n\n```bash\ntailscale up \\\n  --advertise-exit-node \\\n  --advertise-routes=88.88.88.0/24\n```\n\nHowever, this route should **not** be approved or enabled in Headscale.\n\nThe purpose of advertising this route is not to distribute it as a subnet route to other clients.\n\nThe purpose is only to make the local `tailscaled` instance on `node1` treat this subnet as an allowed destination network, so that it does not drop inbound packets received from `node2`.\n\nAs long as the route is not approved in Headscale, it will not be distributed to clients as a subnet route.\n\nTherefore, when `node1` is not selected as an exit node, traffic to `88.88.88.0/24` will continue to use the normal Internet route.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4439510460/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4439583139","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/1637#issuecomment-4439583139","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/1637","id":4439583139,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz888AAAABCJ6pow","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T09:45:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T09:45:00Z","body":"Please open a new issue, this seems intricate so please validate the expected behaviour with Tailscale SaaS aswell so we understand where the issue lies. Ensure you add all the information that we ask for in full in the issue template, not only what the AI gives you. ","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4439583139/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]